><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Melo</surname><given-names>JV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The molecular biology of chronic myeloid leukemia</article-title><source>Blood</source><year>2000</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>3343</fpage><lpage>3356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11071626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R105"><label>105</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Volpe</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Cignetti</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Panuzzo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuka</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vitaggio</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bran-caccio</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Perrone</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rinaldi</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Prato</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fava</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Geuna</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Pautasso</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Casnici</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Signori</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tonon</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarone</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Marelli</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Fazio</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Saglio</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alternative BCR/ABL splice variants in Philadelphia chromosome-positive leukemias result in novel tumor-specific fusion proteins that may represent potential targets for immunotherapy approaches</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>20